# systemd-tmpfiles(5) declaration for spoloh's /etc configuration directory.
#
# ConfigurationDirectory=spoloh in deploy/spoloh.service does NOT do this for
# us: systemd.exec(5) creates that directory root-owned at
# ConfigurationDirectoryMode= (default 0755) regardless of the unit's User=/
# Group=, so relying on it left the service unable to write the config file
# it seeds on first boot. /etc/spoloh must exist, owned by spoloh, before the
# unit starts.
#
# Install alongside the service unit, e.g. by copying this file to
# /usr/lib/tmpfiles.d/spoloh.conf (or /etc/tmpfiles.d/spoloh.conf for a local
# override) and running:
#
#   systemd-tmpfiles --create spoloh.conf
#
# This must run after deploy/spoloh.sysusers (the spoloh user/group have to
# exist first) and before deploy/spoloh.service is first started.
#
# Type Path         Mode  User    Group   Age  Argument
d      /etc/spoloh  0750  spoloh  spoloh  -
